    "noteT106": "T106: tufts, shrub and leaf samples are built of curved cards (ProcMesh::CurvedCard, CardTuft, CardShrub, CardConifer); a cards sample is the bare curved card and, beside it, the plant of its 'plant' entry. T46 integration: grass_*, shrub_small and leaf_* carry layers.foliage (translucency, per-instance and macro colour variation, crown normal blend, alpha by mip). Grass patches are merged meshes, so their normalBlend stays 0 (the sphere centre is the object pivot).",
    "noteT107": "T107: the tufts are instances now (one pivot per tuft: per-tuft colour and occlusion; normalBlend stays 0 on grass, the cards are thin and stand apart). layers.foliage adds baseOcclusion, occlusionHeight (metres over the pivot; the ground is the patch top for tufts and the bush), interiorOcclusion and backlightSpread. The conifer's trunk is bark2.",
